---
import GuideLayout from '../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      "headline": "Best Cafes and Coffee Shops to Work Near Ubud with Fast WiFi and Power Outlets",
      "description": "A field-tested review of quiet coffee shops and cafes for remote workers and digital nomads around Ubud and Tegallalang, Bali.",
      "image": "https://kukacoffee.id/assets/images/customers-1.webp",
      "author": {
        "@type": "Organization",
        "name": "KUKA Coffee Team"
      },
      "publisher": {
        "@type": "Organization",
        "name": "KUKA Coffee Shop",
        "logo": {
          "@type": "ImageObject",
          "url": "https://kukacoffee.id/assets/images/logo.webp"
        }
      },
      "datePublished": "2026-09-08",
      "dateModified": "2026-09-08"
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Are there good cafes to work from north of Ubud?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. Areas like Tegallalang offer quieter open-air cafes with fast 5G WiFi and power outlets, avoiding the scooter traffic and crowded tables of central Ubud."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do cafes in Tegallalang have reliable WiFi?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Specialty spots like KUKA are equipped with modern 5G WiFi and power access at every table specifically built for remote laptop work."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
};
---

<GuideLayout
  title="Best Cafes to Work Near Ubud: Fast WiFi, Quiet Tables & Great Coffee"
  description="Finding a productive place to open your laptop around Ubud isn't just about good coffee—it comes down to stable internet, available sockets, and escaping the scooter noise."
  badge="Bali Remote Work Guide"
  updatedDate="September 2026"
  canonical="https://kukacoffee.id/guides/best-cafes-to-work-near-ubud"
  schema={schema}
  currentPath="/guides/best-cafes-to-work-near-ubud"
>
  <!-- Quick Comparison Table (Above the fold) -->
  <section class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-primary font-headline-sm mb-4">At a Glance: Top Work Cafes Around Ubud</h2>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto border border-outline-variant/40 rounded-xl shadow-sm">
      <table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
        <thead class="bg-surface-container-low text-primary border-b border-outline-variant/30">
          <tr>
            <th class="p-3.5 font-bold">Cafe</th>
            <th class="p-3.5 font-bold">Area</th>
            <th class="p-3.5 font-bold">WiFi & Sockets</th>
            <th class="p-3.5 font-bold">Best For</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-outline-variant/20 bg-surface">
          <tr class="bg-primary/5">
            <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-primary">KUKA Coffee Shop</td>
            <td class="p-3.5 text-on-surface-variant">Tegallalang (North Ubud)</td>
            <td class="p-3.5 text-secondary font-semibold">Fast 5G / Plentiful Sockets</td>
            <td class="p-3.5">Deep focus sessions & rice terrace views</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-primary">Gangga Coffee</td>
            <td class="p-3.5 text-on-surface-variant">Andong Road</td>
            <td class="p-3.5 text-on-surface-variant">Stable WiFi / Good Sockets</td>
            <td class="p-3.5">AC indoor work & video calls</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-primary">Zest Ubud</td>
            <td class="p-3.5 text-on-surface-variant">Penestanan</td>
            <td class="p-3.5 text-on-surface-variant">Decent WiFi / Limited Sockets</td>
            <td class="p-3.5">Social work & plant-based dining</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-primary">Seniman Coffee</td>
            <td class="p-3.5 text-on-surface-variant">Ubud Center</td>
            <td class="p-3.5 text-on-surface-variant">Fast WiFi / Busy outlets</td>
            <td class="p-3.5">Specialty coffee tasting & short work</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Content Sections -->
  <article class="space-y-8 text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">
    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-primary font-headline-sm mb-3">The Common Frustrations with Working in Downtown Ubud</h2>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Central Ubud is packed with great roasteries and coffee spots, but anyone who has spent a week working remotely here knows the drill: tight two-person tables, baristas shouting orders over motorbike traffic, and hunting for the one working wall socket in the back corner.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you have a critical sprint or need three hours of uninterrupted flow, heading 20 minutes north toward Tegallalang gives you open pavilions, cleaner air, and much more breathing room between tables.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- KUKA Feature -->
    <section class="bg-surface-container-low p-6 rounded-2xl border border-outline-variant/30">
      <span class="text-xs uppercase font-bold text-secondary tracking-wider">Top Pick Coffee Shop for Focus & Space</span>
      <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-primary font-headline-sm mt-1 mb-3">1. KUKA Coffee Shop (Tegallalang)</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Located just minutes from the Tegallalang rice terraces, <a href="/" class="text-primary font-bold underline hover:text-secondary">KUKA</a> was built specifically to solve the work-from-cafe trade-off in Bali: you get open-air tropical views without sacrificing work essentials.
      </p>
      <ul class="space-y-2 mb-4 text-sm">
        <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><strong>WiFi:</strong> High-speed 5G connectivity suited for heavy uploads and calls.</li>
        <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><strong>Power Access:</strong> Dedicated outlets at each table.</li>
        <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><strong>Coffee:</strong> 100% single-origin Arabica from Munduk &amp; Kintamani (1,350m altitude), extracted fresh on professional espresso machinery.</li>
        <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><strong>Noise level:</strong> Low ambient breeze and natural valley sounds.</li>
      </ul>
      <a href="/#location" class="inline-block bg-primary text-white text-xs uppercase font-semibold px-4 py-2 rounded hover:bg-primary-container transition-colors">See Location & Hours</a>
    </section>

    <!-- Other Cafes -->
    <section>
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-primary font-headline-sm mb-2">2. Gangga Coffee Gallery (Andong)</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        On the main road heading north out of Ubud, Gangga is a dependable favorite for nomads who prefer air conditioning. The indoor room is well-shielded from road noise, and the internet is consistently stable for client calls.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-primary font-headline-sm mb-2">3. Zest (Penestanan)</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Zest is famous for its massive open structure and vegan menu. It is an inspiring space for creative brainstorming or light laptop tasks, though you will want to arrive early in the morning if you need a table close to a wall outlet.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Practical Tips Section -->
    <section class="border-t border-outline-variant/30 pt-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-primary font-headline-sm mb-3">Tips for Working from Cafes in Bali</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-sm">
        <li><strong>Peak Hours:</strong> 11:00 AM to 2:00 PM is when most cafes get busy with lunch crowds. Early mornings (7:30 AM to 10:30 AM) are the quietest hours for deep work.</li>
        <li><strong>Power Adapters:</strong> Indonesia uses standard European two-pin plugs (Type C and F). Most modern work cafes have these directly built in.</li>
        <li><strong>Scooter Parking:</strong> Always choose cafes with dedicated on-site parking off the main road to avoid traffic congestion.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </article>

  <!-- CTA Box -->
  <div class="mt-12 p-8 bg-primary text-white rounded-2xl text-center">
    <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-2">Planning your work day in Tegallalang?</h3>
    <p class="text-white/80 max-w-md mx-auto mb-6 text-sm">
      Visit KUKA for fresh single-origin coffee, reliable power, and a peaceful open-air space overlooking the rice terraces.
    </p>
    <a class="bg-surface text-primary font-bold text-xs uppercase px-6 py-3 rounded shadow hover:bg-surface-container transition-colors" href="/#location">Get Directions to KUKA</a>
  </div>
</GuideLayout>
